# Dienogest + 10 DMSO: XTB2 MD, spherical confinement
# Starting geometry: Dienogest_Opt_trj.xyz (48 atoms) - the file as provided
#   also already contained a 10-DMSO block, but it reused the same
#   Apixaban-scale DMSO placement/Cell Sphere seen elsewhere in this project
#   (offset 12.78 Ang, sphere radius 14.0 centered at Apixaban's old
#   centroid). That is not appropriate for Dienogest, which is smaller than
#   Apixaban (max atom-centroid distance 6.24 Ang vs Apixaban's 9.03 Ang):
#   20 of the 100 DMSO atoms ended up outside the 14.0 Ang sphere (up to
#   15.14 Ang from center).
#
# This version rebuilds the 10 DMSO placement for Dienogest:
#   - Sphere/placement center = Dienogest's own centroid (31.021, -20.109,
#     -0.926).
#   - Each DMSO placed at offset 10.0 Ang from that centroid, along the same
#     12 directions used throughout this project, with the molecule rotated
#     so its bulk points radially outward.
#   - Cell Sphere radius set to 15.5 Ang (larger than the 10-11 Ang used for
#     the smaller Adamantanol/Phenanthroline solutes, since Dienogest is
#     bigger).
# Checked: min DMSO-Dienogest atom distance = 3.40 Ang (no clash), max atom
#   distance from the sphere center = 13.77 Ang (safely inside the 15.5 Ang
#   sphere). Total atom count = 148 (48 + 10x10), verified.

! XTB2 MD

%md
  Timestep 1.0_fs
  Initvel 298.15_K
  Thermostat NHC 298.15_K Timecon 20.0_fs
  Cell Sphere 31.021, -20.109, -0.926, 15.5 Spring 20
  Dump Position Stride 100 Filename "Dienogest_10DMSO_XTB.xyz"
  Run 20000
end

